Z||000006||Sootah||07-07-2001||02:34 AM||||Winamp has sound quality adjustments, you can turn it from full to half, and 1/4. My question is how do you plan on controlling this thing? You wont have a monitor or anything.. So splain plz.||||reg||1
Z||000007||pHoOl||07-07-2001||01:39 PM||||Alrighty, some explainations...<P>Yeah, a pentium 75 will play full quality ones no prob.  (that's where i got this idea, my last machine was a p75.)  the processor that i have for this project now is a 486DX4 100mHz.  It would not play mp3 at full quality, so i thought i was sunk, but when i was at work i played with converting them to diff quality levels, and foudn that the full quality ( 44kHz and 128Kbs) worked best when used in just mono instead of stereo.  It doesn't sound bad at all, can hardly tell the diff.  <P>As for controlling it.  I have a winamp plugins, (well, three of them that will work together) that will open the player upon booting, scan for mp3 in the cdrom, then add them all to the playlist and start playing.  there is another option to program keys for controlling the diff functions, and i plan on buying either the smallest possible keyboard i can find, or one of those accounting ones that only has the right hand side numbers.  Then, custom program those to do all the playing functions, and even one to shut down windows if i can.  <P>It won't have a monitor hookup, but that's no big deal to me, no room in a fiero to put one anyway, and what could a 486 do for visualization?  not much!  I have heard that there are ways to hook up a little lcd display (similar to a calculator) to the parallel port that will show song title and such.  I don't think i need that as of now, maybe in version two when i have money to spend on this project.  <P>For power, i was going to try to find a DC power supply for a computer, but haven't found one yet, so i was going to use a cheap little inverter from best buy.  I think you can get them for  like 40 bucks now.  <P>For the case, i was going to try to build a custom box out of plexi glass that would be just big enough to fit everything and let some air through.  Thought of mounting it either under that pass side dash, or behind the pass side seat.  Problem with behind the pass seat is that i'm not sure i can get all the cards that run perpendicular to the motherboard to fit under the seat so that the seat doesn't have to be like two feet forward.  If anyone knows about converters that would allow me to plug an ISA card into the board parallel, lemme know.  (Seen them for PCI, but that doens't help me much yet)<P>I think this answers all the questions, let me know if you guys have anymore.  I'd be glad to publish designs once it's done if anyone would be interested.  <P>Oh, as for using a pentium laptop... yeah, it would be easier, but i don't have one, and they cost money.  Checked ebay, i think they're like 300.  Which, at that point, may as well just buy the kenwood car deck that would play mp3.<P><P>------------------<BR>Rice mobiles are like tampons... Every p@#%y has one.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>       <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/phoolsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
